   "evidence": "A grep for `lowerOrderL_homMul|homMul.*lowerOrder` in code/TauCeti hits only Perturbation.lean:118 and :157 (uses of the two together, no lemma). The proof of `zeroOneLowerOrdersL_perturbationSuccL` (Perturbation.lean:169-195) works through `chartValueL_perturbationSuccL_ae` at both orders instead.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Geometry/Manifold/VectorBundle/Sobolev/HomMultiplication/Higher.lean",
   "fix": "Add a public `lowerOrderL_homMulSuccL`: `(A.ofBaseSet h).sectionChartData.lowerOrderL volume q (k+1) (homMulSuccL (k := k+1) \u03b1 \u03be) = homMulSuccL (k := k) (lowerOrderL \u03b1) (lowerOrderL \u03be)`, proved from `chartValueL_homMulSuccL_ae` and `chartValueL_coe_lowerOrderL`. Then derive `zeroOneLowerOrdersL_perturbationSuccL` from it together with `zeroOneLowerOrdersL_zeroOnePartSobolevL`.",
   "issue": "`homMulSuccL` has no lemma for how it interacts with order lowering, the operation it is used with downstream. Because `perturbationSuccL_apply` is `@[simp]` and unfolds to `zeroOnePartSobolevL (homMulSuccL \u03b1 (lowerOrderL \u03be))`, `simp` gets stuck on `zeroOneLowerOrdersL` of that term, and `zeroOneLowerOrdersL_perturbationSuccL` has to redo the chart calculation instead of rewriting.",
   "line": 191
  }
